{"type":"assistant","uuid":"06cae5e9-91ae-4808-831e-3767161b542e","session_id":"e651c352-cd9f-4882-ad7c-3a0da86f7ba4","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"06cae5e9-91ae-4808-831e-3767161b542e","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is verified and the project compiles successfully.\n\n## Bug Fix Summary\n\n**Root Cause:** In `Whiteboard.java`, the boolean flag `mUndoModeActive` is set to `true` whenever a stroke is drawn (`drawFinish()`) and reset to `false` only when the whiteboard is cleared (`clear()`). However, when the user undoes all strokes via the undo button, `mUndoModeActive` is never reset back to `false`.\n\n**Flow of the bug:**\n1. User draws → `mUndoModeActive = true`, `undoSize() = 1` → undo button shows eraser icon, enabled\n2. User undoes → `mUndoModeActive = true` (stays!), `undoSize() = 0` → `prepareOptionsMenu()` fires, sees `isUndoModeActive() == true` and `undoSize() == 0`, so disables the button\n3. User redraws → `mUndoModeActive = true`, `undoSize() = 1`, but `prepareOptionsMenu()` is **not** called (it's only triggered on menu recreation, not on touch events) → menu retains stale disabled state\n4. Result: eraser button remains grayed out\n\n**Fix:** In `Whiteboard.undo()`, when the undo queue becomes empty (`undoSize() == 0`), reset `mUndoModeActive = false` and call `supportInvalidateOptionsMenu()`. Also trigger menu refresh on non-empty undo stacks so the state is always consistent after an undo."}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":33817,"output_tokens":342,"cache_read_input_tokens":32736,"total_tokens":34159}}}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","uuid":"541637da-7fc6-4216-add4-888a0330fb3e","session_id":"e651c352-cd9f-4882-ad7c-3a0da86f7ba4","is_error":false,"duration_ms":139571,"duration_api_ms":62678,"num_turns":3,"result":"The fix is verified and the project compiles successfully.\n\n## Bug Fix Summary\n\n**Root Cause:** In `Whiteboard.java`, the boolean flag `mUndoModeActive` is set to `true` whenever a stroke is drawn (`drawFinish()`) and reset to `false` only when the whiteboard is cleared (`clear()`). However, when the user undoes all strokes via the undo button, `mUndoModeActive` is never reset back to `false`.\n\n**Flow of the bug:**\n1. User draws → `mUndoModeActive = true`, `undoSize() = 1` → undo button shows eraser icon, enabled\n2. User undoes → `mUndoModeActive = true` (stays!), `undoSize() = 0` → `prepareOptionsMenu()` fires, sees `isUndoModeActive() == true` and `undoSize() == 0`, so disables the button\n3. User redraws → `mUndoModeActive = true`, `undoSize() = 1`, but `prepareOptionsMenu()` is **not** called (it's only triggered on menu recreation, not on touch events) → menu retains stale disabled state\n4. Result: eraser button remains grayed out\n\n**Fix:** In `Whiteboard.undo()`, when the undo queue becomes empty (`undoSize() == 0`), reset `mUndoModeActive = false` and call `supportInvalidateOptionsMenu()`. Also trigger menu refresh on non-empty undo stacks so the state is always consistent after an undo.","usage":{"input_tokens":771853,"output_tokens":10397,"cache_read_input_tokens":593472,"total_tokens":782250},"permission_denials":[]}
